# LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is the Windows default, and it hands out CRLF working
# copies of files stored as LF. Two things here break under that:
#
#   1. `llms-full.txt` is GENERATED, and CI checks it for drift by comparing it
#      against a fresh run of the generator. The generator emits LF. A CRLF
#      working copy therefore differs on every line, so the check fails on a
#      Windows clone that has changed nothing. Observed, not hypothetical.
#
#   2. Test fixtures and the `.slurp` sources under `examples/` are compared as
#      bytes in several places.
#
# Declaring it here means the setting is a property of the repository rather
# than of each contributor's git config, so nobody has to know.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Genuinely binary, and must never be touched by any conversion. The wasm is
# built rather than committed; the entry is here so that an accidental commit
# of a build artifact cannot be corrupted silently.
*.wasm binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.woff2 binary
